What it is:
A consent-agenda resolution (item 6.I) from the June 20, 2024 meeting appointing the Troy School District's districtwide Professional Development Advisory Committee.

The appointment:
- The Board appoints Natalie Haezebrouck and members of the Teaching and Learning Department as committee representatives.

Why it matters (State School Aid Act Section 101(10)):
To count professional development toward instructional hours, "qualifying" PD must:
- Align with the school/district improvement plan under which it is provided;
- Link to one or more criteria of the district's teacher evaluation tool;
- Be MDE-approved as counting for State Continuing Education Clock Hours (SCECHs);
- Total no more than ten combined hours before the first / after the last scheduled school day;
- Total no more than ten hours in a single month;
- Include at least 75% of the teachers scheduled to participate.

Recommended action:
Accept the resolution (Yes/No vote lines blank in this copy).
